<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16755" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄσῡλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>safe from violence,
				inviolate,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεὶ πᾶν ἐστιν ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Parm.
					8.48
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μενεῖς ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					728
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκπεμπέτω ἄσυλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					866d
				</span></i>
			; of the persons of magistrates, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				7.45
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				10.39
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἄ.</span>
			<i>right of sanctuary</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>GDI</u>
				4940.13
			</span></i>(<span class="entity">Allaria</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>not liable to reprisals</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῦλαι</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				9(1).333
			</span></i> (
				Locr.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> c. gen.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γάμων ἄ.</span>
			<i>safe from</i> marriage, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				61
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of places,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆν ἄ παρασχεῖν</span> make the
			land <i>a refuge,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Med.</u>
				387
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱερὸν ὃ ἄσυλον νενόμισται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					4.18.10
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				635.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				1053ii9
			</span></i><span class="entity">(i B. C.)</span>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄσυλον,
					τό,</span>
			<i>sanctuary,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				304.28
			</span></i>: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόμον τηρεῖν ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>OGI</u>
					383.115
				</span></i>
			 (Commagene, <span class="entity">i B. C.</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ.
				γράμματα, στῆλαι,</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				8.110
			</span></i>; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόμην ἄ. φυλάξαι</span>”
				<i>uncut,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VA</u>
					4.16
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
